# Changelog

> Before the core parsing and demuxing implementation moved to `libaribtlv` on
> 2026-08-05, the project used the `tlvdemux` namespace. Those entries are
> labelled **legacy `tlvdemux` implementation**; this is a historical name,
> not a separate product line.

## [0.3.4] - 2026-08-29

- Add public video-unavailable resilience modes, switch buffer requirements to
  audio after three failed forward RAP recoveries, and restore video only after
  a later RAP produces a compositor-presented frame.
- Add bounded recorded and live transition contracts, runtime
  `activeSourceBuffers` verification, and a stable `TLV_VIDEO_UNAVAILABLE` demo
  status without changing the video-stage geometry.
- Keep explicit recorded seeks at the exact requested `currentTime` when the
  target lies in damaged video: extend the final pre-damage frame or duplicate
  the first stable RAP as a still filler, while preserving continuous AAC and
  the original RAP timestamps.
- Reuse the formally landed demuxer without a second reposition, rescan, or
  expansion of the shared 16 MiB budget; unify the demo module versions and fix
  recovery-logger initialization before accessing its controller.

## [0.3.3] - 2026-08-28

- Define the automatic dual-video recording timeline as the union of the
  preferred and rainfall presentation ranges, expose its start and end, and use
  the same origin for duration, startup, explicit seek, and MSE timestamps.
- Execute a concrete selected-layer playback-damage seek exactly once, while
  retaining damage found during prefetch until playback reaches it or stalls.
- Keep AAC output continuous across recoverable source damage and prevent video
  damage from resetting an independent audio timeline, avoiding Chromium
  `DEMUXER_UNDERFLOW` on the captured recording.

## [0.3.2] - 2026-08-28

- Atomically map a fresh recorded playback's first common A/V interval to
  timestamp zero before installing either SourceBuffer, without changing the
  media-element clock.
- Preserve explicit rainfall splice offsets, and defer
  `MSE_STARTUP_NO_COMMON_AV` until the 16 MiB startup budget is exhausted when
  no common A/V entry can be formed.

## [0.3.1] - 2026-08-28

- Give live playback its own flow-control entry so a valid first common A/V
  interval can start later than timestamp zero, then align the media clock only
  after the configured live startup buffer is ready.
- Keep the 16 MiB no-progress limit when a live stream cannot form any common
  A/V interval, and add direct regression coverage for both successful live
  alignment and bounded failure.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-08-28

- Add public browser SDK modules for bounded recorded seek, MSE output queues,
  track/layer selection, strict recorded Range sources, duration probing, live
  input coalescing, playback-damage recovery, and Worker RPC.
- Migrate the demo to those public modules and remove its duplicated lifecycle
  helpers. Package publication remains an explicit release action; the batch
  stays incomplete until the documented DPlayer npm cutover and acceptance.
- Preserve caller-owned `Uint8Array` inputs at the Worker boundary so recorded
  seek probe/landing cache reuse cannot fail on a detached `ArrayBuffer`.
- Make manual-rainfall to automatic selection actively restore a healthy
  preferred paired A/V layer at the next usable RAP, supersede unfinished manual
  switches, and map a pre-entry manual switch to the startup playback entry.

## [0.2.4] - 2026-08-26

Commit range: `7aa53cb..HEAD`

- Add Annex-B HEVC colour and HDR static-metadata parsing, and update the
  `libaribtlv` integration to 0.6.0 with timestamp/fMP4 regression coverage.
- Optimize WebGPU HLG-to-SDR conversion with a native 3D LUT and hardware
  trilinear sampling, while documenting why metadata-only reinterpretation is
  not a valid browser tone-mapping path.
- Expose IP data flows, transport NTP clocks, TLV network and address-map
  tables, raw signalling, unknown descriptors, and signalling messages through
  the WASM/TypeScript API and JSON inspector output.

## [0.2.3] - 2026-08-19

Commit range: `2e93df2..7aa53cb`

- Add normal playback controls, seek calculation tooling, and related regression
  coverage.
- Improve HDR presentation policy, video signalling, static metadata handling,
  and colour analysis.
- Add MSE output capability, format, and state handling across the worker and
  WASM modules.

## [0.2.2-rc1] - 2026-08-15

Commit range: `1adff6b..HEAD`

- Add HLG-SDR video signalling control, including live stream property updates
  and SDR reinterpretation that preserves BT.2020 primaries and matrix.
- Add C++/WASM HLG-SDR tone-mapping LUTs and a WebGPU luminance-only renderer
  for correcting SDR content carried in HLG without independently boosting RGB
  channels.
- Add native, WASM, and sample-based regression coverage for the colour path.

## [0.2.1] - 2026-08-15

Commit range: `e960417..1adff6b`

- Ignore recoverable filler bytes before the first validated TLV packet so
  startup resynchronization does not become an MSE error.
- Keep AAC decode time contiguous across missing frames, and reinitialize MSE
  audio when a LATM StreamMuxConfig changes, including 5.1 ↔ stereo transitions.
- Add regression coverage for initial TLV resynchronization, AAC forward
  timestamp gaps, repeated audio configuration changes, and sample-based WASM
  audio configuration switching.

## [0.2.0] - 2026-08-15

Commit range: `7c47b47..55796ec`

- Introduce dedicated HEVC/AAC MSE track muxers, Chromium coded-frame policy
  tests, safer cross-layer seeking, and playback-damage reporting and recovery
  guidance.
- Expand VideoToolbox diagnostics and refine video-layer reprobe and seek
  behavior for broadcast playback.

## [0.1.11] - 2026-08-14

Commit range: `239cb25..9a34f78`

- Add richer subtitle metadata, subtitle rendering and selection, audio
  asset-group selection, coordinated video/audio layer switching, staging, and
  synchronization.

## [0.1.10] - 2026-08-14

Commit range: `4e353a4..60369de`

- Consolidate command-line tools into a unified executable and improve static
  linking.
- Preserve HEVC colour information in MP4 output and add MSE audio-track
  switching with splice events.

## [0.1.9] - 2026-08-11

Commit range: `3c6d800..e232e11`

- Add the `tlvanalyze` and `tlvdemux-pipe` tools plus native build/release
  automation.
- Move the core parsing and demuxing implementation into `libaribtlv`, then
  migrate `tlvdemux` integration to the `aribtlv` public types and namespace.

## [0.1.8] - 2026-08-03

Commit range: `d1ff955..ed55f37`

- Harden MSE timing and coded-frame handling: drop non-advancing DTS, cut
  fragments at safe composition boundaries, preserve source timescales, and
  prevent invalid leading HEVC pictures from reaching decoders.
- Correct ARIB B60 access-unit timestamp derivation, leap-second anchoring,
  subtitle reference-time validation, and MPU consistency checks.

## [0.1.7] - 2026-08-03

Commit range: `49c5a63..73451a1`

- Add `MseAppendQueue`, SourceBuffer lifecycle finalization, media-segment
  validation, and a browser queue example.

## [0.1.6] - 2026-08-03

Commit range: `4b7e9e1..18f44e4`

- Add viewer-participation notifications, MPT/MH-AIT snapshots, MH-SDT/MH-TOT
  parsing, extended events, and related data-broadcast support.

## [0.1.5] - 2026-08-01

Commit range: `c187e51..e66a821`

- Coalesce live-stream reads and document and measure WASM input and memory
  behavior for improved playback throughput.

## [0.1.4] - 2026-08-01

Commit range: `ab4f4a6..4cdc744`

- Add a WebKit media-plane fallback, improve MSE callback handling and demo
  documentation, and refine keyboard and viewport behavior.

## [0.1.3] - 2026-08-01

Commit range: `3363bdc..7b47136`

- Expand ARIB signalling support and enable `ManagedMediaSource` for Safari
  demos.

## [0.1.2] - 2026-08-01

Commit range: `eaef4cf..27cd7ae`

- Add stream events, subtitle passthrough, application descriptors and
  profiles, plus data-broadcast caption integration.

## [0.1.1] - 2026-07-31

Commit range: `c06b2f8..e4684b0` — **legacy `tlvdemux` implementation**

- Add WASM demo playback, seeking and range support; introduce initial HEVC MSE
  remuxing, live-start buffering, RASL handling, VideoToolbox probing, and
  recording seek support.
- Add application-resource management, broadcast clock and program events,
  broadcast-resource handling, and B62 subtitle resources and timing metadata.

## Initial development - 2026-07-19 to 2026-07-30

Commit range: `050f800..02e6b9b` — **legacy `tlvdemux` implementation**

- Establish the MMT/TLV demuxer, compressed-IP and MMTP parsing, service
  selection, timestamp mapping, resource limits, CMake packaging, CLI
  inspection, audio metadata, recording indexing, and seek primitives.
- Add B62 subtitle resources and timing metadata, application/data-asset
  parsing and extraction, decompression, duration probing, and the initial
  Emscripten/WASM bindings.
